I am an engineer and researcher based in Paris. Currently, I work at [Datadog](https://www.datadoghq.com/) as a Staff Applied Scientist.

# Experience

Previously, I was:
*   Cofounder and CSO at _Sarus Technologies_ (YC W22), working on privacy-preserving data science - _acquired by Datadog in 2025_
*   Senior Director Data Scientist at _Verizon Media_
*   Founder and CSO at _AlephD_, providing real-time solutions for publishers - _acquired by Verizon in 2016_
*   Quantitative Risk Management at _Société Générale_
*   Economic and Financial Advisor at the _French Treasury_

# Publications

I have published research on stochastic control, auction optimization, and privacy.

*   [Recurrent Neural Networks for Stochastic Control in Real-Time Bidding](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3292500.3330691) (KDD 2019)
*   [Optimal Allocation of Real-Time-Bidding and Direct Campaigns](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3219819.3219826) (KDD 2018)
*   [Optimization of a SSP's Header Bidding Strategy using Thompson Sampling](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3219819.3219886) (KDD 2018)
*   [Real-Time Optimization of Web Publisher RTB Revenues](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3097983.3098008) (KDD 2017)
*   [The Strange Complexity of Constrained Delaunay Triangulation](http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~jrs/papers/nptet.pdf)

